# Global input hints

Grid Dungeon uses one **bottom-right** overlay (`InputHintPresenter`, `Assets/UI/Screens/Shared/InputHint.uxml`, `sortingOrder` **300**) for **input bind copy** — what the player can press **right now**.

Design reference: [shared menu & picker UI § Global input hints](../../docs/04-dev/shared-menu-picker-ui.md#global-input-hints), [input bindings § Global input hints](../../docs/02-systems/input-bindings.md#global-input-hints).

## Global strip — input binds only

**Publish only** keyboard/mouse **verbs**: key or button name + action (`Z Confirm`, `W/S Row`, `L Log`, `M Fullscreen`, `Esc Pause`).

## Segment order (locked)

Every bind segment in `TabbedPickerRailHints` (game repo: `Assets/Scripts/UI/Views/TabbedPickerRailHints.cs`) uses this order:

1. **Z and X** — confirm/cancel first (`Z Confirm · X Cancel`)
2. **W/S and Q/E** — navigation axes next; **W/S before Q/E** when both apply (`W/S Command · Q/E Tab`)
3. **Other keys** — L, Esc, M, Click, … last (`L Log · Esc Pause`)

Separate segments with ` · ` (middle dot + spaces). **Do not** hardcode hint strings in views — add a constant or helper on `TabbedPickerRailHints`.

| OK on global strip | Not on global strip |
|--------------------|---------------------|
| `Z Confirm · X Cancel · W/S Command · L Log` | Party cell, facing arrow, HP/MP, floor name |
| `Z Confirm · X Back · Q/E Tab · W/S Row` | Tutorial lore, quest text, warnings |
| `Z Pick · X Back · Q/E Member · W/S Slots` | `north up`, map legend, focused slot names (`· Weapon`), confirm-target labels |

**Do not** put bind copy on panel footers, picker chrome, command rail, map title row, or victory overlays — use `InputHints.Publish(gameState, text)` / `Clear` instead.

**Constants:** `TabbedPickerRailHints` (+ screen-specific `DismissHint` where Runtime cannot reference UI). One authoritative string per context; no duplicated UXML `Label` hints for the same binds.

## Publishers (extend this list, do not fork a second strip)

| Phase / overlay | Owner |
|-----------------|--------|
| Hub | `HubHudView.RefreshInputHint` / `RestoreInputHint` |
| Combat | `CombatHudView.RefreshInputHint` / `RestoreInputHint` |
| Party menu | `PartyMenuOverlayView.RefreshMenuHint` |
| Exploration minimap | `ExplorationMapCoordinator.RefreshGlobalInputHint` |
| Exploration pause / party menu | `PartyMenuOverlayView.RefreshMenuHint` (`ExplorationPauseMenuShell` on exploration shell) |
| Story modal | `StoryEventView` (`TabbedPickerRailHints.ModalDismiss`) |
| Victory rewards | `BattleRewardScreenView` on show / clear on dismiss |
| Floor transition | `FloorTransitionPresenter` clears on start; `ExplorationMapCoordinator` / `HubHudView` republish on `PresentationReleased` |
| Story end / pause close | `InputRouter` restores phase hint via `RestoreGlobalInputHintForPhase` |

Clear on overlay close, phase exit, or when a higher-priority overlay owns binds. Restore the underlying screen hint after dismiss (hub `RestoreInputHint`, exploration `ExplorationMapCoordinator.RefreshGlobalInputHint`, combat `CombatHudView.RestoreInputHint`, etc.).

## Modal panel hints (`hud-overlay__hint`)

**Exploration pause**, quit confirm, and similar **full-screen overlays** may keep **non-bind** copy on the modal (`Progress since your last inn save…`) — that is **not** global input-hint content.

When a modal’s **only** footer text is bind copy (`Esc Resume`), prefer **global** `InputHints` while the modal is open instead of a duplicate `hud-overlay__hint`.

## Implementation checklist

1. New screen with keyboard/mouse binds → add/extend `TabbedPickerRailHints` (or documented constant), publish from one view method, clear on close.
2. **Segment order** — new copy follows Z/X → W/S & Q/E → other keys; mirror the table in [shared-menu-picker-ui.md § TabbedPickerRailHints copy](../../docs/04-dev/shared-menu-picker-ui.md#tabbedpickerrailhints-copy).
3. Removing a legacy footer hint → delete UXML `Label` + USS; wire publisher + input-handler block while overlay open.
4. PR review: if `InputHintPresenter` text is not a bind line, move status/tutorial to HUD labels or modal body — not the global strip.
5. PR review: reject hint strings that reorder segments (e.g. `L Log` before `Z Confirm`) or duplicate bind footers on panels.
